# authorized_keys — timelapse_tunnel @ dedicated tunnel sshd (TCP/22022)
#
# Canonical authority: froekjaer/timelapse-pro → deploy/ssh/authorized_keys.timelapse_tunnel
# Installed to: /etc/ssh/timelapse-tunnel/authorized_keys (root:wheel 0644; root-only write)
#
# POLICY:
#   * One dedicated keypair PER EDGE DEVICE. Never shared. Never the API-mTLS
#     key. Private keys live only on their Edge.
#   * Every entry MUST use this exact option prefix:
#         restrict,port-forwarding,permitlisten="127.0.0.1:<port>"
#     Semantics (sshd(8), AUTHORIZED_KEYS):
#       restrict         → disables EVERYTHING, including all forwarding;
#       port-forwarding  → re-enables port forwarding (this is what turns
#                          forwarding back on — permitlisten does NOT do that);
#       permitlisten=…   → narrows remote (-R) listening to exactly this
#                          loopback address:port on the headend.
#     Without the port-forwarding option, a restrict+permitlisten-only entry
#     can establish NO forwards at all (silent tunnel failure).
#     authorized_keys options can
#     only restrict below sshd_config, never broaden it.
#   * Entries are provisioned at Edge cutover (separate phase), e.g.:
#
# restrict,port-forwarding,permitlisten="127.0.0.1:2201" ssh-ed25519 AAAA…placeholder… TL-C87FF9587CA0
# restrict,port-forwarding,permitlisten="127.0.0.1:2204" ssh-ed25519 AAAA…placeholder… TL-043EB9E72EFD
#
# This template intentionally contains NO valid keys.
